{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 5,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.046,
            0.367,
            0.064
          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.085,
            0.761,
            0.11
          ],
          "content": "? Find the parity of the number of small squares in these grids:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.182,
            0.121,
            0.328,
            0.193
          ],
          "content": "(a) $2 7 \\times 1 3$ (b) $4 2 \\times 7 8$ (c) $1 3 5 \\times 6 5 4$"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.209,
            0.418,
            0.232
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Parity of Expressions"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.241,
            0.847,
            0.281
          ],
          "content": "Consider the algebraic expression: 3n + 4. For different values of n, the expression has different parity:"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.186,
            0.288,
            0.811,
            0.403
          ],
          "content": "| n | Value of 3n + 4 | Parity of the Value |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 3 | 13 | odd |\n| 8 | 28 | even |\n| 10 | 34 | even |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_5_table_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.418,
            0.73,
            0.473
          ],
          "content": "Come up with an expression that always has even parity. Some examples are: 100p and 48w – 2. Try to find more."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.478,
            0.7,
            0.504
          ],
          "content": "Come up with expressions that always have odd parity."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.518,
            0.847,
            0.559
          ],
          "content": "？ Come up with other expressions, like 3n + 4, which could have either odd or even parity."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.575,
            0.848,
            0.616
          ],
          "content": "？ The expression 6k + 2 evaluates to 8, 14, 20,... (for k = 1, 2, 3,...) — many even numbers are missing."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.634,
            0.832,
            0.687
          ],
          "content": "？ Are there expressions using which we can list all the even numbers? **Hint:** All even numbers have a factor 2."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.694,
            0.785,
            0.718
          ],
          "content": "? Are there expressions using which we can list all odd numbers?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.726,
            0.849,
            0.785
          ],
          "content": "We saw earlier how to express the n<sup>th</sup> term of the sequence of multiples of 4, where n is the letter-number that denotes a position in the sequence (e.g., first, twenty third, hundred and seventeenth, etc.)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.788,
            0.848,
            0.828
          ],
          "content": "？ What would be the n<sup>th</sup> term for multiples of 2? Or, what is the n<sup>th</sup> even number?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.836,
            0.474,
            0.856
          ],
          "content": "Let us consider odd numbers."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.861,
            0.469,
            0.884
          ],
          "content": "What is the 100th odd number?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.89,
            0.745,
            0.912
          ],
          "content": "To answer this question, consider the following question:"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.938,
            0.194,
            0.955
          ],
          "content": ""
        },
